1
00:00:14,040 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the sunset floating
over the Nakagawa River,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,900
kicking a pebble, flying on the momentum,

3
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:29,360
to Kashiwa,
the type who was always joking around,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,800
they laughed at me for staying
just as cheerful as ever.

5
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:37,440
Even if I drop my energy somewhere,

6
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:38,680
it's locked up tight, no matter what.

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,940
A nightmare,
one thing: the unchanging streetscape

8
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:43,900
is gentler than ever.

9
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:46,860
Because the crows are cawing,

10
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:48,920
the day is ending, isn't it?

11
00:00:49,820 --> 00:00:51,940
Yakitori Honbari.

12
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:54,640
Seeing it too

13
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:57,460
Of the pointed hat,

14
00:00:58,460 --> 00:01:04,080
retiring from people... the sunset sinks.

15
00:01:06,860 --> 00:01:10,080
Tomorrow too, dropping it all,
it'll end, won't it?

16
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:12,800
If you don't know the magazine,
you're happy, they say.

17
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:16,300
I'm a fool who only
realized after losing it.

18
00:01:24,600 --> 00:01:27,400
Because I just don't want to do it!

19
00:01:39,440 --> 00:01:40,800
See you.

20
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:43,980
The four duty reports are due tomorrow,
remember.

21
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:46,980
Don't you dare forget.

22
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:48,500
Ugh, you're so annoying.

23
00:01:49,060 --> 00:01:51,560
Yeah, yeah, yeah, I know.

24
00:01:51,560 --> 00:01:51,820
Hey.

25
00:01:51,820 --> 00:01:54,260
Ugh.

26
00:01:56,620 --> 00:01:57,540
Absolutely.

27
00:01:57,540 --> 00:01:58,640
It's due tomorrow, got it?

28
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:01,560
Ugh.

29
00:02:02,420 --> 00:02:03,340
That said,

30
00:02:08,140 --> 00:02:10,780
Secrets like this are worthless to me.

31
00:02:10,780 --> 00:02:12,060
Damn it!

32
00:02:12,060 --> 00:02:14,960
My backdoor scheme failed too, after all.

33
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:18,400
Nakagawa-kun,

34
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:19,980
What is it?

35
00:02:23,060 --> 00:02:25,280
Don't go shoving your work onto others!

36
00:02:28,480 --> 00:02:30,200
Hey, hey, Reiko-chan.

37
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:33,200
What is it, Ryo-chan?
Stop using that creepy voice.

38
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:39,060
Don't go luring people with gifts.
Place your own bets properly.

39
00:02:41,820 --> 00:02:43,740
I just can't shake this feeling.

40
00:02:54,740 --> 00:02:55,920
Don't draw attention.

41
00:03:01,540 --> 00:03:02,340
Kress

42
00:03:10,405 --> 00:03:14,060
My room's such a mess, I can't concentrate.

43
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:15,140
That's it!

44
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:18,260
That's it!

45
00:03:18,260 --> 00:03:19,300
It has to be!

46
00:03:19,300 --> 00:03:21,543
Alright, there, alright, done!

47
00:03:21,593 --> 00:03:23,710
Ah there...

48
00:03:23,760 --> 00:03:25,672
Toss, toss, heave-ho,

49
00:03:25,722 --> 00:03:28,220
heave, heave, heave

50
00:03:28,220 --> 00:03:30,278
Okay, there, whew,

51
00:03:30,328 --> 00:03:33,373
who'd think this was my room? There.

52
00:03:33,423 --> 00:03:37,157
let's keep this momentum
and do the reports too,

53
00:03:37,207 --> 00:03:39,100
No, the cassette...

54
00:03:41,700 --> 00:03:45,440
Uh, hmm

55
00:03:53,140 --> 00:03:55,000
after all that tidying up,

56
00:03:56,540 --> 00:03:58,580
yeah, yeah,
it's better when it's this messy,

57
00:03:58,580 --> 00:04:00,820
it really looks like I'm working!

58
00:04:01,660 --> 00:04:03,800
Atmosphere is what matters, atmosphere!

59
00:04:18,440 --> 00:04:19,320
That's right.

60
00:04:20,720 --> 00:04:23,420
I knew something was missing:
a late-night snack.

61
00:04:23,420 --> 00:04:26,740
I'll wolf it down and get this done quickly.

62
00:04:37,660 --> 00:04:40,160
Tonton-tonton-ton.

63
00:04:40,160 --> 00:04:41,440
Alright, then.

64
00:04:41,440 --> 00:04:43,700
Just vegetables won't do

65
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:45,420
Something more...

66
00:04:47,840 --> 00:04:49,780
Chashu, menma, narutomaki.

67
00:04:49,780 --> 00:04:51,500
Guess if you look,
there's plenty to be found.

68
00:04:54,440 --> 00:04:55,480
Tuna, that's it.

69
00:04:55,480 --> 00:04:56,680
Let's throw this in too.

70
00:04:57,340 --> 00:04:58,060
Alright, and this too.

71
00:04:58,960 --> 00:05:00,400
Let's add this as well.

72
00:05:01,140 --> 00:05:02,020
Mm...

73
00:05:04,020 --> 00:05:04,260
Yeah, I knew it.

74
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:07,280
For the finishing touch,
it's gotta be pepper.

75
00:05:10,620 --> 00:05:12,880
Senpai, what are you doing?

76
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:14,880
Perfect timing.

77
00:05:14,880 --> 00:05:16,460
Want some too?

78
00:05:18,260 --> 00:05:19,260
No, thanks.

79
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:20,460
I see.

80
00:05:20,460 --> 00:05:22,280
Well then, I'm digging in.

81
00:05:26,100 --> 00:05:28,220
Delicious, as expected of me!

82
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:30,800
I really am superhuman.

83
00:05:32,100 --> 00:05:35,400
Maybe I should have made
something with a bit more substance.

84
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:39,200
I forgot about that.

85
00:05:45,360 --> 00:05:49,060
Now that I think about it, I feel
like I haven't done laundry in a while.

86
00:05:54,580 --> 00:05:56,400
So I let it pile up this much?

87
00:05:56,400 --> 00:06:00,140
Laundry, laundry, laundry,
and then all at once...

88
00:06:05,840 --> 00:06:07,060
Right, then.

89
00:06:08,520 --> 00:06:10,660
That's right, I need to tidy up the closet.

90
00:06:10,660 --> 00:06:12,820
I've been thinking that for a while.

91
00:06:14,420 --> 00:06:16,200
What a mess, isn't it?

92
00:06:16,200 --> 00:06:19,340
I was going to put it out
with the recyclables, though.

93
00:06:26,040 --> 00:06:28,900
Man, Kochikame is still funny no
matter how many times I read it.

94
00:06:28,900 --> 00:06:31,940
No, no, I need to hurry up and get to work.

95
00:06:32,480 --> 00:06:34,620
Alright, tidying up, tidying up.

96
00:06:34,620 --> 00:06:35,860
This one.

97
00:06:36,740 --> 00:06:40,940
Model gun, Colt Python .357 Magnum, 4-inch.

98
00:06:40,940 --> 00:06:43,940
I never get tired of admiring this beauty.

99
00:06:43,940 --> 00:06:45,420
Looks like it's starting to rust a little.

100
00:06:45,420 --> 00:06:48,280
Heave-ho, heave-ho, heave-ho.

101
00:06:48,280 --> 00:06:50,540
Wait, I was in the middle of tidying up,
wasn't I?

102
00:06:51,260 --> 00:06:56,840
Whoa, a nostalgic dart from the shaved
ice eating contest at the shopping street.

103
00:06:56,840 --> 00:06:57,760
Nah!

104
00:06:59,020 --> 00:07:00,520
My skills haven't faded

105
00:07:01,620 --> 00:07:04,160
It's a jigsaw, the legendary masterpiece.

106
00:07:04,160 --> 00:07:06,560
A camel crossing the Sahara Desert.

107
00:07:06,560 --> 00:07:08,680
The ultimate 12,000 pieces.

108
00:07:09,180 --> 00:07:11,560
I bought this back when I was obsessed with puzzles,
didn't I?

109
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:13,220
So nostalgic, so nostalgic.

110
00:07:13,900 --> 00:07:14,420
Here we go.

111
00:07:14,420 --> 00:07:16,780
This one's hard.

112
00:07:16,780 --> 00:07:18,060
So this goes here.

113
00:07:18,060 --> 00:07:18,480
Alright.

114
00:07:19,400 --> 00:07:19,940
Here we go.

115
00:07:24,180 --> 00:07:25,280
Done!

116
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:25,960
Aaaaaah.

117
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:36,060
...
Well, hey.

118
00:07:36,060 --> 00:07:39,400
Good morning, you there.

119
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:40,440
Whoa.

120
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:56,860
I'll do it once this is done.

121
00:07:56,860 --> 00:07:59,960
Ugh, Ryo-chan,
you're starting something new again?

122
00:08:00,720 --> 00:08:01,740
Reiko.

123
00:08:01,740 --> 00:08:05,760
No, now that I look at it,
this police box is pretty filthy, isn't it?

124
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:10,180
Hey, you're the one who always makes the mess,
so what are you talking about?

125
00:08:10,180 --> 00:08:11,980
It's an escape, it's just avoidance.

126
00:08:11,980 --> 00:08:14,180
Just because you don't
want to write your reports.

127
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:18,560
Oops, I did it.

128
00:08:19,120 --> 00:08:19,920
Here too.

129
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:24,620
Good morning.

130
00:08:25,860 --> 00:08:26,860
What's going on here?

131
00:08:26,860 --> 00:08:28,000
Chief.

132
00:08:28,680 --> 00:08:29,820
Ryotsu, today is -

133
00:08:29,820 --> 00:08:33,880
Speaking of which, the wall out front...

134
00:08:35,060 --> 00:08:35,460
The wall.

135
00:08:35,460 --> 00:08:36,400
No, this...

136
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:44,380
What is that Ryotsu doing?

137
00:08:44,380 --> 00:08:47,780
He still hasn't finished today's reports,
you know.

138
00:08:48,300 --> 00:08:51,920
He's forcing himself to find other work to put off the reports,
isn't he.

139
00:08:52,340 --> 00:08:52,740
What?

140
00:08:57,500 --> 00:08:59,240
Can't you tidy up a little?

141
00:09:00,180 --> 00:09:00,960
Yeah, yeah.

142
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:04,420
If only every day could be like this,

143
00:09:06,700 --> 00:09:10,200
wait, if I'm making a mess like
this just to avoid paperwork,

144
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:13,520
then if I always keep
Ryotsu busy with paperwork,

145
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:17,220
couldn't I keep things
like this all the time?

146
00:09:18,720 --> 00:09:20,000
Yes, perfect!

147
00:09:23,700 --> 00:09:25,180
You're still here?

148
00:09:25,180 --> 00:09:27,940
Ryotsu, what about the reports due today?

149
00:09:29,040 --> 00:09:30,620
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

150
00:09:33,500 --> 00:09:35,500
By the way,

151
00:09:35,500 --> 00:09:40,020
just as I thought.

152
00:09:41,360 --> 00:09:43,440
How are the reports coming along?

153
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:54,040
Just as I thought.

154
00:09:54,040 --> 00:09:55,860
As long as I give him paperwork,

155
00:09:55,860 --> 00:09:57,340
Ryotsu will work.

156
00:09:58,500 --> 00:09:59,460
Ryotsu.

157
00:09:59,460 --> 00:10:00,980
You've cleaned up nicely

158
00:10:04,140 --> 00:10:05,620
Well, never mind that.

159
00:10:05,620 --> 00:10:07,980
Those reports are due today, you know.

160
00:10:08,720 --> 00:10:09,980
And I need you to handle this too.

161
00:10:09,980 --> 00:10:11,120
While you're at it, this as well.

162
00:10:11,120 --> 00:10:13,420
And then there's the
backlog of incident reports.

163
00:10:19,340 --> 00:10:22,140
Got it, Ryotsu?

164
00:10:22,140 --> 00:10:26,120
Then I'm counting on you.
I'm heading to the station.

165
00:10:26,980 --> 00:10:28,280
Damn it.

166
00:10:28,280 --> 00:10:34,160
You two are going out too?

167
00:10:34,160 --> 00:10:36,040
On patrol.

168
00:10:36,040 --> 00:10:38,800
Well, Ryo-chan, take care.

169
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:40,460
Well then, senpai, we're off.

170
00:10:42,460 --> 00:10:43,060
Aaaahhh.

171
00:10:44,180 --> 00:10:47,880
Aaaahhh.

172
00:10:47,880 --> 00:10:54,120
It's still not clean enough. Alright,
I'll go all out and do a thorough job!

173
00:10:54,120 --> 00:11:02,020
Aaaahhh. It's cleaner than ever now

174
00:11:02,020 --> 00:11:05,920
Right?

175
00:11:05,920 --> 00:11:09,094
Well, I'll put this off for later,

176
00:11:09,144 --> 00:11:11,160
guess I'll start with the new stuff.

177
00:11:13,020 --> 00:11:14,540
A survey?

178
00:11:16,980 --> 00:11:22,620
Baseball tournament sign-ups?
Senior citizens' club? Elementary schoolers?

179
00:11:23,520 --> 00:11:24,900
W-what is this?

180
00:11:29,360 --> 00:11:32,040
I get it, Chief Ohara!

181
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:37,440
He planted all this on
purpose just to make me clean!

182
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:38,560
Damn it!

183
00:11:40,680 --> 00:11:43,660
I wonder if Senior Ryotsu
finished his reports properly.

184
00:11:44,340 --> 00:11:47,900
Who knows.
He's probably too absorbed in cleaning.

185
00:11:47,900 --> 00:11:51,620
Well, I suppose it's a
stroke of luck in disguise.

186
00:11:51,620 --> 00:11:54,380
Who'd have thought Ryotsu
would be cleaning up?

187
00:11:57,020 --> 00:11:57,780
What?

188
00:12:02,980 --> 00:12:07,080
Look, Chief,
I've tidied everything up nicely.

189
00:12:07,780 --> 00:12:08,260
This.

190
00:12:08,260 --> 00:12:12,820
You wanted me to clean up,
didn't you, Chief?

191
00:12:12,820 --> 00:12:17,740
So I've sorted everything at
the police box by material.

192
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:19,400
Yo!

193
00:12:20,100 --> 00:12:21,540
You idiot!

194
00:12:21,540 --> 00:12:25,020
But you started it first, Chief!

195
00:12:28,420 --> 00:12:30,100
In the end, you hadn't done it.

196
00:12:32,940 --> 00:12:35,280
Defender of justice, Ryo-san.

197
00:12:38,320 --> 00:12:41,160
Oh no, the money, there's no money left!

198
00:12:43,060 --> 00:12:46,180
That's it,
I'm going to find a new part-time job!

199
00:12:46,180 --> 00:12:47,700
Ryo-chan, again?

200
00:12:47,920 --> 00:12:51,540
Senpai,
it hasn't even been a week since payday!

201
00:12:52,760 --> 00:12:54,500
There you are, Ryo-san.

202
00:12:55,280 --> 00:12:56,760
Everyone from the next town?

203
00:12:56,760 --> 00:13:00,580
No, actually,
we have a job in mind for you, Ryo-san.

204
00:13:02,040 --> 00:13:04,060
It's a part-time job only you can do.

205
00:13:04,060 --> 00:13:06,040
A part-time job, you say?

206
00:13:06,100 --> 00:13:08,400
Come with us for a moment, would you?

207
00:13:10,900 --> 00:13:12,100
What an amazing tree.

208
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:14,600
So there was a tree like this.

209
00:13:15,420 --> 00:13:17,740
It's already over 180 years old.

210
00:13:18,340 --> 00:13:19,060
Back in the day, you know,

211
00:13:19,060 --> 00:13:22,540
this was a plaza like
a paradise for children.

212
00:13:22,540 --> 00:13:23,060
This place was

213
00:13:25,460 --> 00:13:26,020
But then

214
00:13:26,740 --> 00:13:29,020
gradually fewer and fewer
children came to play,

215
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:31,040
and the land was sold off bit by bit,

216
00:13:32,320 --> 00:13:35,340
until only this tree was left.

217
00:13:35,340 --> 00:13:37,340
How truly sad.

218
00:13:42,460 --> 00:13:45,400
Well, enjoy admiring it
to your heart's content.

219
00:13:46,340 --> 00:13:48,660
Ryo-san, don't you dare go home.

220
00:13:48,660 --> 00:13:51,380
Because it has nothing to do with me.

221
00:13:51,380 --> 00:13:53,300
From now on, it's your job, Ryo-san.

222
00:13:53,820 --> 00:13:57,080
This land has been put up for auction.

223
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:02,140
So a contractor is trying
to cut down this tree.

224
00:14:02,140 --> 00:14:04,860
Ryo-san, that's a terrible story, isn't it?

225
00:14:06,540 --> 00:14:08,640
It's in the way,
so why not just cut it down?

226
00:14:10,440 --> 00:14:11,620
Oh my.

227
00:14:11,620 --> 00:14:14,440
To us, it's a treasure.

228
00:14:14,440 --> 00:14:15,300
I see.

229
00:14:16,900 --> 00:14:21,160
Ryo-san, if you manage to protect it,
we'll pay you a reward.

230
00:14:22,300 --> 00:14:23,620
So, how much?

231
00:14:24,300 --> 00:14:26,340
30,000 yen a day.

232
00:14:32,280 --> 00:14:35,260
What a fortunate neighborhood this is.

233
00:14:35,260 --> 00:14:37,840
If it weren't for a man like me,

234
00:14:37,840 --> 00:14:40,680
the life of this poor, innocent giant tree

235
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:43,060
Thank you, Ryo-san.

236
00:14:43,060 --> 00:14:45,000
So how are we going to protect it?

237
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:49,220
If you keep watch from up in the tree
and drive off the construction crew,

238
00:14:49,220 --> 00:14:51,460
Now listen carefully.

239
00:14:51,460 --> 00:14:55,120
Ryo-san, you can't do it in your uniform.

240
00:14:57,080 --> 00:14:59,280
A police officer can't very
well be protesting, can he?

241
00:14:59,720 --> 00:15:02,000
When it comes to tree climbing,
it has to be this.

242
00:15:05,840 --> 00:15:09,040
Dressed like that,
people will think you're fooling around.

243
00:15:10,080 --> 00:15:11,800
Poi! That's the one.

244
00:15:12,560 --> 00:15:16,460
A stimulant, a helmet,
and a helper, and it's perfect.

245
00:15:17,320 --> 00:15:18,520
Settled, settled!

246
00:15:19,140 --> 00:15:21,220
Alright!

247
00:15:21,920 --> 00:15:23,300
Leave it to you, Ryo-san.

248
00:15:23,820 --> 00:15:25,120
Leave it to me.

249
00:15:27,180 --> 00:15:29,300
With you on it, it'll be fine.

250
00:15:29,300 --> 00:15:31,680
I've found a great part-time job!

251
00:15:48,160 --> 00:15:50,540
Hey! Don't you dare cut that tree!

252
00:15:51,820 --> 00:15:52,860
What? What's going on?

253
00:15:53,220 --> 00:15:54,980
Go home, go home! The lot of you!

254
00:15:55,700 --> 00:15:59,380
What's that?
Never mind, let's just get on with the job.

255
00:15:59,880 --> 00:16:01,760
Damn it, you're ignoring me?

256
00:16:01,760 --> 00:16:03,540
Alright, if it's come to this -

257
00:16:08,620 --> 00:16:09,880
You punks!

258
00:16:10,520 --> 00:16:13,300
Come near me and you won't get off lightly.

259
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:17,960
Quietly go home,
or I'll keep sitting right here.

260
00:16:17,960 --> 00:16:19,420
Brace yourselves.

261
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:23,720
My natural speaking voice is no joke,
you know.

262
00:16:26,080 --> 00:16:27,620
Serves you right!

263
00:16:34,900 --> 00:16:35,700
So bored.

264
00:16:36,680 --> 00:16:38,620
I wonder if those guys will come back.

265
00:16:39,480 --> 00:16:40,840
I'm getting hungry, too.

266
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:42,200
Ryo-san!

267
00:16:42,820 --> 00:16:43,960
Ryo-san!

268
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:45,640
We brought you breakfast.

269
00:16:45,640 --> 00:16:47,000
Thanks!

270
00:16:47,740 --> 00:16:48,880
Wow!

271
00:16:49,580 --> 00:16:51,140
Sorry we're late.

272
00:16:51,140 --> 00:16:52,460
Go ahead and eat up.

273
00:16:52,460 --> 00:16:55,800
It's a special bento everyone in
the neighborhood association made.

274
00:16:55,800 --> 00:16:58,100
There's tea and juice too.

275
00:16:58,520 --> 00:17:00,800
Hey, look at all this!

276
00:17:02,360 --> 00:17:03,080
Thanks for the food!

277
00:17:03,080 --> 00:17:06,700
This morning,
we heard Ryo-san driving those guys off.

278
00:17:07,260 --> 00:17:09,380
I see, I'm really helping out

279
00:17:09,380 --> 00:17:11,820
Asking Ryo-san was the right call.

280
00:17:14,260 --> 00:17:15,620
Well, good luck to you then.

281
00:17:15,620 --> 00:17:18,040
If you want anything, just say so.

282
00:17:18,040 --> 00:17:19,774
Three meals a day with snacks,

283
00:17:19,824 --> 00:17:22,680
if this kind of part-time job lasts until retirement,
that's something.

284
00:17:24,220 --> 00:17:26,440
Look who's back. Go home, go home!

285
00:17:26,440 --> 00:17:28,760
You're the one who should come down.

286
00:17:29,300 --> 00:17:31,360
We've already been granted
permission to cut it down.

287
00:17:31,360 --> 00:17:34,720
I'm not coming down!
My livelihood is on the line here!

288
00:17:35,500 --> 00:17:35,900
Livelihood?

289
00:17:36,500 --> 00:17:38,560
My livelihood is on the line too, you know.

290
00:17:39,120 --> 00:17:40,840
Alright, here we go, right here!

291
00:17:41,400 --> 00:17:42,297
Here,

292
00:17:42,347 --> 00:17:45,820
in this quiet residential
area of Katsushika Ward,

293
00:17:45,820 --> 00:17:49,860
a precious tree that the local residents
dearly love is about to be cut down.

294
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:51,540
Is that the TV? Good.

295
00:17:52,020 --> 00:17:53,400
Good people across the nation,

296
00:17:54,120 --> 00:17:57,900
these cruel people are
trying to cut down this tree.

297
00:17:58,480 --> 00:18:01,520
Should something like this be allowed?

298
00:18:04,680 --> 00:18:05,800
Please take a look.

299
00:18:05,800 --> 00:18:09,260
A champion of justice is doing
his best to protect the tree.

300
00:18:10,340 --> 00:18:11,880
All you people of good sense,

301
00:18:12,360 --> 00:18:14,900
justice will always win!

302
00:18:24,740 --> 00:18:27,360
Whoa, wow, what's all this?

303
00:18:27,360 --> 00:18:29,500
It's a gift for Ryo-san.

304
00:18:30,940 --> 00:18:34,400
Support presents are pouring
in from all over the country.

305
00:18:35,060 --> 00:18:38,340
Yay, getting this much for free!

306
00:18:38,340 --> 00:18:40,960
Keep up the good work, Ryo-san!

307
00:18:41,440 --> 00:18:43,340
Coming, coming, here you go!

308
00:18:53,180 --> 00:18:55,020
It's like a secret base or something.

309
00:18:55,020 --> 00:18:58,200
More stuff keeps coming,
and life is getting better!

310
00:19:05,220 --> 00:19:07,800
Alright, let's show everyone
we're champions of justice.

311
00:19:07,800 --> 00:19:09,500
We need even more stuff!

312
00:19:10,880 --> 00:19:15,840
Everyone gathered here,
can we just let this outrage pass?

313
00:19:15,840 --> 00:19:20,660
Even if I'm alone,
I will fight to protect this tree.

314
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:22,000
Come on, come on!

315
00:19:22,560 --> 00:19:23,500
Don't give up!

316
00:19:24,800 --> 00:19:29,820
For me, fighting alone,
your support is what keeps me going.

317
00:19:29,820 --> 00:19:31,700
Relief supplies over here!

318
00:19:31,700 --> 00:19:38,140
Where did he get that costume?

319
00:19:39,500 --> 00:19:42,040
Studying like that is just what
you'd expect from a senior officer.

320
00:19:42,040 --> 00:19:45,440
Mr. Champion of Justice,
we have a delivery for you.

321
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:53,860
Thanks for your hard work!

322
00:19:58,920 --> 00:20:02,320
It's really piling up,
there's no room left to put anything!

323
00:20:02,320 --> 00:20:04,800
These branches are in the way, aren't they?

324
00:20:04,800 --> 00:20:08,000
It's a big tree, so nobody down below
will notice if we trim a few branches.

325
00:20:09,500 --> 00:20:12,800
That's more room. While I'm at it,
let me expand the floor too.

326
00:20:14,540 --> 00:20:18,280
If we split the wiring from here,
we'll have electricity too, no problem.

327
00:20:31,900 --> 00:20:33,780
Ryo-san, it's over.

328
00:20:33,900 --> 00:20:34,700
Good work.

329
00:20:34,860 --> 00:20:35,300
What?

330
00:20:35,860 --> 00:20:37,400
This tree has been saved.

331
00:20:37,540 --> 00:20:37,980
Thank you.

332
00:20:40,020 --> 00:20:41,620
But once I'm gone,

333
00:20:41,620 --> 00:20:43,520
they're bound to come back.

334
00:20:44,260 --> 00:20:46,980
This morning we got notice that
the construction has been cancelled.

335
00:20:47,400 --> 00:20:48,560
Don't believe it.

336
00:20:48,560 --> 00:20:50,100
That's just their trick.

337
00:20:50,100 --> 00:20:51,720
They surely won't come back now, right?

338
00:20:52,320 --> 00:20:54,040
No, this is where the climax begins!

339
00:20:54,040 --> 00:20:56,200
We can't come down yet, not by a long shot.

340
00:20:56,720 --> 00:20:57,580
Ryo-san.

341
00:20:58,100 --> 00:21:00,480
And bring 50 kilos of rice too.

342
00:21:00,480 --> 00:21:01,900
We're also out of water.

343
00:21:01,900 --> 00:21:03,900
Make it 100 liters of mineral water, okay?

344
00:21:03,900 --> 00:21:04,740
Yoroshiku!

345
00:21:08,480 --> 00:21:10,520
Looks like we've been set up.

346
00:21:10,520 --> 00:21:13,500
Getting Ryo-san to leave
is becoming the harder job.

347
00:21:14,560 --> 00:21:16,520
This tree is starting to
look like a devil's tree.

348
00:21:16,520 --> 00:21:18,120
Let's keep watch over this tree.

349
00:21:18,120 --> 00:21:20,660
If the contractors don't show up,
the part-time job is off.

350
00:21:25,140 --> 00:21:27,400
Are they planning to post a lookout?

351
00:21:28,020 --> 00:21:30,220
Looks like the contractors really gave up.

352
00:21:30,880 --> 00:21:33,420
Geez, what a bunch of spineless wimps.

353
00:21:34,740 --> 00:21:37,480
If I don't do something,
my shift will be over.

354
00:21:38,060 --> 00:21:39,460
Should I try that trick?

355
00:21:40,120 --> 00:21:41,100
Get out of the way, you!

356
00:21:41,700 --> 00:21:42,960
I won't let them cut it down,
no matter what.

357
00:21:42,960 --> 00:21:44,860
If you're going to cut it, cut me first!

358
00:21:44,860 --> 00:21:45,760
What?

359
00:21:47,240 --> 00:21:48,240
Hurry up.

360
00:21:48,240 --> 00:21:49,560
How about this?

361
00:21:53,680 --> 00:21:55,760
No way, I'm not leaving the tree.

362
00:21:55,760 --> 00:21:57,840
Let's call it a day for now.

363
00:21:58,620 --> 00:22:00,340
The contractors really came.

364
00:22:00,340 --> 00:22:02,640
Putting your body on the
line to protect the tree,

365
00:22:06,580 --> 00:22:07,880
you've really done well.

366
00:22:07,880 --> 00:22:10,140
Here's 3,000 yen each.

367
00:22:10,680 --> 00:22:11,000
Thank you very much.

368
00:22:13,140 --> 00:22:16,040
You could be a bit rougher, you know.

369
00:22:16,040 --> 00:22:17,700
Well, see you tomorrow.

370
00:22:17,700 --> 00:22:18,140
At 8 o'clock.

371
00:22:24,520 --> 00:22:26,560
A bath after work is the best.

372
00:22:26,560 --> 00:22:28,800
There's no way I'm quitting
such an easy part-time job.

373
00:22:28,800 --> 00:22:30,440
300,000 yen for 10 days.

374
00:22:30,440 --> 00:22:31,660
60,000 yen for 2 days.

375
00:22:32,640 --> 00:22:33,520
Three days would be 90,000 yen.

376
00:22:34,320 --> 00:22:36,060
And my life is fulfilling too.

377
00:22:36,180 --> 00:22:38,180
Maybe I should just move in here.

378
00:22:45,740 --> 00:22:47,320
Too much electricity use

379
00:22:49,660 --> 00:22:50,300
Fire!

380
00:22:51,720 --> 00:22:52,600
This one too!

381
00:22:54,220 --> 00:22:56,360
It's a waste, but it's mineral water!

382
00:22:58,480 --> 00:23:00,040
It's no good. Escape!

383
00:23:06,360 --> 00:23:08,040
Our tree...

384
00:23:08,040 --> 00:23:09,400
How could they do such a thing...

385
00:23:09,400 --> 00:23:12,840
It wasn't me!
It was an accident, an accident!

386
00:23:13,740 --> 00:23:15,260
Hey, Ryo-san!

387
00:23:16,180 --> 00:23:18,560
The tree's gone. What happened?

388
00:23:19,300 --> 00:23:20,300
He's dead!

389
00:23:20,300 --> 00:23:26,100
The tree-felling contractor's
job has been called off?

390
00:23:26,100 --> 00:23:29,220
You told us to come at eight every morning,
didn't you?

391
00:23:29,220 --> 00:23:32,660
We're taking today's 3,000 yen day pay.

392
00:23:34,500 --> 00:23:37,600
Th-that's why, no that...

393
00:23:38,100 --> 00:23:38,940
Ryo-san!

394
00:23:38,940 --> 00:23:40,980
That's why, escape!

395
00:23:40,980 --> 00:23:44,040
Oi, wait!

396
00:23:59,220 --> 00:24:01,840
I walked looking back over my shoulder

397
00:24:01,840 --> 00:24:04,460
as Mom held my hand

398
00:24:05,580 --> 00:24:07,700
The feeling I had back then,

399
00:24:08,740 --> 00:24:11,760
that strange feeling

400
00:24:12,480 --> 00:24:13,180
so

401
00:24:13,180 --> 00:24:16,900
on the tiles of the shopping arcade,

402
00:24:16,900 --> 00:24:19,020
only on the black ones,

403
00:24:19,020 --> 00:24:22,660
I tried walking on them.

404
00:24:25,200 --> 00:24:28,900
Everyone was a child once,

405
00:24:29,220 --> 00:24:30,940
but everyone has forgotten.

406
00:24:32,020 --> 00:24:34,980
Politicians with their self-important faces

407
00:24:34,980 --> 00:24:38,260
and the aunties with blue eyeshadow

408
00:24:38,260 --> 00:24:41,280
should try turning the corner.

409
00:24:42,080 --> 00:24:43,880
That corner,

410
00:24:45,100 --> 00:24:49,060
and you'll get to meet everyone, everyone.

411
00:24:51,200 --> 00:24:53,840
Over there is the Camera Rally,

412
00:24:54,880 --> 00:24:57,200
surely the Camera Rally,

413
00:24:58,460 --> 00:25:02,220
everyone, come to our town!

414
00:25:02,220 --> 00:25:06,900
Over there is Kameari,

415
00:25:08,260 --> 00:25:10,180
surely Kameari,

416
00:25:11,460 --> 00:25:15,480
everyone, come to our town!

417
00:25:16,460 --> 00:25:16,980
Thank you.

418
00:25:20,140 --> 00:25:21,340
Damn it!

419
00:25:21,560 --> 00:25:22,840
That Naoko!

420
00:25:22,900 --> 00:25:26,560
How dare you print my embarrassing
photo in the in-house newsletter!

421
00:25:27,200 --> 00:25:28,480
Because of you, I've become a laughingstock!

422
00:25:28,780 --> 00:25:30,060
In that case, as revenge,

423
00:25:30,060 --> 00:25:33,220
I'm going to get some great
embarrassing photos of Naoko!

424
00:25:33,600 --> 00:25:35,960
Next time: Naoko's unexpected day!

425
00:25:36,560 --> 00:25:37,200
See you then!

